# what the four images (pages, api, video, dummy) are built from, as git pathspecs.
#
# the images are named after the last commit that touched one of these: deploy.sh
# (`image_commit`) asks the registry for that tag, ship.sh builds and tags with it,
# and .github/workflows/images.yml builds and pushes it (its `paths:` filter is the
# same list, written out by hand: a workflow filter cannot read a file). a commit that
# touches none of these (docs, deploy.sh, docker-compose.yml) has no images of its own
# and runs the ones before it, so nothing is recreated for it.
#
# one pathspec per line. `#` starts a comment. the caddyfile is bind-mounted, in no image.
api
video
frontend
:(exclude)frontend/Caddyfile
Cargo.toml
Cargo.lock
.dockerignore
.github/workflows/images.yml
